        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The Founders intended public service to be temporary, not lifelong.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Historically, public servants returned to farms, businesses, or other civilian roles after serving.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The American Revolution was partly motivated by opposition to entrenched professional political classes and monarchical bureaucracies.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
